# Build context exclusions for the three service images
# (apps/{api,worker,web}). All three are built with the REPO ROOT as the context
# and `-f apps/<svc>/Dockerfile`.
#
# This lives at the REPO ROOT on purpose: buildx reads .dockerignore from the
# CONTEXT, and a per-app copy would be ignored entirely.
#
# WHAT MUST NOT BE LISTED HERE
#   package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, tsconfig.base.json
#     The workspace install resolves @pr-agent/* through these. Excluding any of
#     them makes `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` fail outright, or silently
#     produce a different dependency graph than the one CI's gate verified.
#   apps/*/package.json
#     Same reason: pnpm links workspace packages from these manifests, so the
#     manifest list in each Dockerfile has to be complete.
#   apps/api/drizzle/, apps/*/dist/
#     apps/api's Dockerfile copies dist/ from the BUILDER stage, never from the
#     context, so host build output must not leak in. A stale host dist/ shipped
#     into an image would masquerade as a fresh build.
#   pnpm-workspace.yaml's allowBuilds
#     Removing the file removes the only record of which dependency build
#     scripts are permitted, and the install fails with ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS.

# Dependencies — always reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile. Sending
# them also risks copying absolute paths from a machine that is not this one.
node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/node_modules

# Version control / CI — hundreds of MB, and it busts the layer cache on every
# unrelated commit.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.moon
.hermes

# Build and tool output — regenerated inside the image.
dist
**/dist
.next
out
*.tsbuildinfo
.moon/cache

# Logs and editor state
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# Local env files. Credentials belong in the environment at `docker run`, never
# baked into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# NOTE: .npmrc is deliberately NOT ignored. It carries the pnpm settings that
# decide what gets installed, so excluding it would change the resolved tree
# without any visible difference in the build log.